{"cluster_id": "C-3500", "topic": "snapshot stream placement", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["B027-034", "B028-018"], "canonical_claim": "`_snap` remains under `stream/` because it is immutable and transaction-addressed, grouped with logs for recovery hints and covered-object cleanup; moving it to `state/` would require a second hot LIST or a simultaneous recovery-and-cleanup redesign. Additionally, `_snap` remains under `stream/` because it is immutable and sequence-addressed, is grouped with logs for recovery hints and covered-object cleanup, and avoids a second hot LIST; the stream/state split is by access pattern, not ownership.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-28-cas-ref-chain-stage-b-catalog.md#task-4d", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-27-cas-ref-chain-complete-cut-design.md#invariants"]}
