{"cluster_id": "C-3515", "topic": "CAS cache wrapping", "target": "architecture/storage-layout", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-286", "B051-061"], "canonical_claim": "`DiskObjectStorageCache::wrapWithCache` must reuse the CAS metadata storage instead of a generic cache-passthrough wrapper because the generic wrapper hides `isContentAddressed` and concrete CAS types used by read and write paths. Additionally, `DiskObjectStorage::wrapWithCache` reuses the CA metadata storage directly instead of wrapping it in the generic `MetadataStorageFromCacheObjectStorage`, because the generic wrapper would hide `isContentAddressed()` and the concrete types the CA read/write paths `dynamic_cast` to, forcing the write path into `NOT_IMPLEMENTED`; only the object storage is cached, control-plane traffic bypasses the cache via the CA storage's own raw object-storage pointer.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/01-architecture.md#g-cache-over-ca-layering", "docs/superpowers/cas/upstream-patch-inventory.md#disk-object-storage-cache-cpp", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/01-frontend.md#g-cache-over-ca-layering"]}
